          "summary": "Two-step sign-in with passkeys or an authenticator app",
          "details_markdown": "Turn it on in Settings → Security. Add a passkey (your fingerprint, face, device PIN or a security key) or an\nauthenticator app, and signing in asks for it after GitHub, Google, X, LinkedIn or Facebook, so a stolen login for one\nof those isn't enough to get into your account and every brand it posts as. You get ten recovery codes in case you\nlose your phone. Making API tokens, approving the CLI, connecting accounts, and setting up webhooks and feeds ask you to\nconfirm it's you again after 15 minutes. The security page also lists where you're signed in, signs out other\nbrowsers, and keeps a log of sign-ins and changes.",
